  "interpretation": {
    "coinbase": "Coinbase operates distinct collateral regimes. The non-US Coinbase Advanced Global Derivatives cross-collateral product lists XRP; Coinbase Prime Global Derivatives for eligible US institutions lists only USDC/BTC/ETH; US Derivatives use USD cash with optional indirect USDC conversion. These must be separate product entities in the feature store.",
    "circle_ripple": "Circle and Ripple are direct product partners for USDC on XRPL and simultaneously compete in stablecoins through USDC and RLUSD. Ripple said it would use USDC alongside RLUSD; treat complementarity and competition as simultaneous, not mutually exclusive.",
    "rebalancing": "Coinbase's non-US cross-collateral documentation permits positive-equity currencies to be used to purchase a negative settlement currency. XRP could be sold in that process if XRP is the positive-equity currency, but this is a conditional mechanical inference; no XRP-specific rebalancing or sale volume is disclosed.",
    "cftc": "CFTC Letter 26-17 is a staff no-action position, not a rule or blanket product authorization. The referenced March 2026 SEC/CFTC digital-commodity interpretation lists XRP. The current public US Prime collateral list still excludes XRP."
